message.content:
Below is a minimal example of an **interactive rotating card** using only HTML and CSS.  
When you hover over the card, it will rotate 180° around its Y‑axis (a “flip” effect).  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* Container holding the card */
.card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D transform */
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth animation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* Enables 3D children */
}

/* Flip the card when hovered */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card .front,
.card .back {
    backface-visibility: hidden;       /* Hide backside during rotation */
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

/* Styling for front side */
.card .front {
    background: #fff;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #333;
}

/* Styling for back side */
.card .back {
    background: #f8f9fa;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);        /* Position behind front */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: #555;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front side -->
        <div class="front">
            <p>Front Side</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back side -->
        <div class="back">
            <p>Back Side</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3D space (`perspective`) so the rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | Holds both sides and performs the rotation. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Each side of the card. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side that should not be visible during rotation. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` | Rotates the card 180 degrees around the Y‑axis. |

Feel free to replace the text or add images inside the `<div class="front">` and `<div class="back">` elements to suit your design. Enjoy!
